# Canonicalize commit authorship without rewriting history.
#
# Early commits were authored under a personal address and under a previous
# employer's domain. Both are already published — including on `refs/pull/*`
# refs that GitHub pins permanently and no force-push can reach — so a history
# rewrite would be destructive and still incomplete. `.mailmap` is the
# supported fix: `git log`, `git shortlog` and GitHub all honour it.
#
# New commits should use the canonical identity directly:
#   git config --local user.name  "Ruben Broekx"
#   git config --local user.email ruben@thinkvelta.ai

Ruben Broekx <ruben@thinkvelta.ai> <broekxruben@gmail.com>
Ruben Broekx <ruben@thinkvelta.ai> <ruben.broekx@boardofinnovation.com>
